  <h1>Zeeshan Farooq</h1>
  <p class="article-meta">Plants Researcher · Author, Simply Plant Care</p>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Zeeshan Farooq is a plants researcher and the author of every guide on
      Simply Plant Care. He researches indoor plant care — watering, light,
      soil, and the common problems that kill houseplants — and turns that
      research into plain, practical guides a beginner can actually follow.
    </p>
    <h2>How he works</h2>
    <p>
      Every guide is written from general horticultural knowledge and
      checked against public references from university extension services
      and botanical gardens. He does not copy content from other websites,
      and he does not invent statistics, studies, or quotes. Where a topic
      is genuinely debated — for example, whether misting raises humidity
      meaningfully — he says so instead of presenting one view as settled
      fact.
    </p>
    <h2>What he writes about</h2>
    <p>
      Watering and light first, because those two things kill most
      houseplants. Then soil and pots, feeding, and fixing specific
      problems: yellow leaves, brown tips, drooping stems, and plants that
      have stopped growing. If a guide is wrong, he corrects it — see our
      <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
